  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5239",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a multifaceted compound that exerts its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18, ultimately leading to the activation of TE-10. Additionally, Mollicellin N is shown to target P2X purinoceptor 1, which is subsequently targeted by a compound that also leads to TE-10. This indicates that Mollicellin N may act through multiple distinct mechanisms to influence TE-10. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, with Mollicellin N potentially serving as a central node in a network of targets that ultimately converge on TE-10. The evidence supports a role for Mollicellin N in modulating TE-10 through diverse molecular mechanisms, underscoring its potential as a key player in the biological response to this compound.",
